        "original_id": "44e61b84-0b4e-5a2b-9f98-86c086e935b2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William Howard, William Small\n- Organizations: Baltimore and Ohio Railroad\n- Places: Maryland, Baltimore, Sandy Hook\n- Roles: American mechanical engineer, architects\n- Buildings: McKim's School\n\nFacts:\n- William Howard was an American mechanical engineer who lived from 1793 to 1834.\n- William Howard was one of the first people to work for the Baltimore and Ohio Railroad.\n- At first, the Baltimore and Ohio Railroad was located entirely in the state of Maryland.\n- The original line of the Baltimore and Ohio Railroad ran from the port of Baltimore west to Sandy Hook.\n- McKim's School was designed by Baltimore architects William Howard and William Small.\n- McKim's School was erected in 1833.",
